quran[11]{c,v,t}:
  39,11,"Say: ‘Indeed, I am commanded to worship Allah, being sincere to Him in devotion and obedience."
  39,12,I am also commanded to be the first of those who submit (to Him).’
  39,13,"Say: ‘Indeed, should I disobey My Lord, I fear the punishment of a tremendous Day.’"
  39,14,"Say: ‘(Only) Allah do I worship, devoting my faith exclusively to Him."
  39,15,"So worship whatever (gods) you wish besides Him.’ Say: ‘Indeed, the (true) losers are the ones who will lose themselves and their families on the Day of Resurrection. Beware! That is the most apparent loss."
  39,16,"There shall be canopies of fire above them and (similar) canopies beneath them. That is how Allah makes His servants fear.’ So, My servants! Be conscious of Me."
  39,17,"And those who stay away from worshipping false gods and turn to Allah (alone) will have good news. So give glad tidings to My servants,"
  39,18,"who listen (attentively) to what is said and follow the best (sense) of it—they are the ones whom Allah has rightly guided, and they are ones who possess intellect."
  39,19,Can he against whom the word of torment has become due (escape punishment)? And can you save someone who is (already) in the Fire?
  39,20,"But those conscious of their Lord will have elevated mansions (with other) lofty abodes built above them, with rivers flowing beneath them. (That is) the promise of Allah. Allah does not break His promise."
  39,21,"Do you not see that Allah sends down rain from the sky and then channels it as springs under the ground? Then, He produces crops of various colours through it. Then they wither, and you see them turning yellow. Then He makes them crushed and broken into pieces. There is indeed a reminder in that for the possessors of intellect."
